\title{Counted arguments are passed borrowed where the caller keeps them}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-10-31}
\author{claude-opus-5-5}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{compiler-runtime}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{864}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Counted arguments are passed borrowed where the caller keeps them (\pr{762}), at every optimizing level. The new \code{\verb~|reussir-borrow-specialization~} pass switches such a call to a private clone of the callee that neither retains nor releases the argument, nor the values loaded through it, so a read-only traversal of retained data updates no counts. Calls at an argument's last use keep the owned callee, so their in-place reuse is unchanged. \code{\verb~|rrc --disable-borrow-analysis~} (and the matching \code{\verb~|disable_borrow_analysis~} profile knob in \code{\verb~|rene~}) turns it off; \code{\verb~|reussir-borrow-analysis-remark~} reports the decisions. Borrowed parameters carry the new \code{\verb~|#reussir.borrowed~} argument attribute, which PJRT donation and UCRA treat as not owned.}

\p{Landed in \pr{864}.}
